# neg08-empty-reconstruction-fails-closed

If the user wants: Poisson reconstruction from estimated normals yields nothing and publishes nothing
(JA) 空の再構成結果は失敗として閉じる

Families: pointset, reconstruction

## Inputs (import first)
- $sphere_points: cgal_artifact_import {"artifact_type": "PointSet3", "path": "tests/fixtures/master/reconstruction/sphere_points.xyz", "unit": "mm"}
(Use your own file of the same artifact type and unit for real work.)

## Steps
1. `pointset.normals.estimate` (estimate): Estimate nonzero point normals using PCA or jet fitting.
   inputs {"points": "$sphere_points"}; parameters {"method": "pca", "neighbors": 12}
2. `pointset.normals.orient_mst` (orient): Orient point normals with CGAL MST propagation.
   inputs {"points": {"slot": "points", "step": "estimate"}}; parameters {"drop_unoriented": false, "neighbors": 12}
3. `reconstruction.poisson` (poisson): Poisson surface reconstruction from an oriented point set: Poisson_reconstruction_function, Poisson_mesh_domain_3 and a surface-only Mesh_3 extraction (closed manifold option) into a triangle surface mesh.
   inputs {"points": {"slot": "points", "step": "orient"}}; parameters {"max_deviation": {"unit": "mm", "value": 3.0}, "sm_angle": 20, "sm_distance": 0.375, "sm_radius": 2}

## cgal_plan request
```json
{"request": {"steps": [{"id": "estimate", "inputs": {"points": "$sphere_points"}, "operation": "pointset.normals.estimate", "parameters": {"method": "pca", "neighbors": 12}}, {"id": "orient", "inputs": {"points": {"slot": "points", "step": "estimate"}}, "operation": "pointset.normals.orient_mst", "parameters": {"drop_unoriented": false, "neighbors": 12}}, {"id": "poisson", "inputs": {"points": {"slot": "points", "step": "orient"}}, "operation": "reconstruction.poisson", "parameters": {"max_deviation": {"unit": "mm", "value": 3.0}, "sm_angle": 20, "sm_distance": 0.375, "sm_radius": 2}}]}}
```

## Expected outcome
Expected REFUSAL/FAILURE (demonstrates fail-closed behaviour): {"code": "EMPTY_RECONSTRUCTION", "stage": "execute", "state": "failed"}

en.recipe/wf11-union-then-difference-chain:
# wf11-union-then-difference-chain

If the user wants: Chained booleans where the second consumes the first
(JA) 和のあとに差を取るBoolean連鎖

Families: mesh, boolean

## Inputs (import first)
- $cube_a: cgal_artifact_import {"artifact_type": "TriangleSurfaceMesh", "path": "tests/fixtures/master/wave_a_boolean/cube_a.off", "unit": "mm"}
- $cube_overlap: cgal_artifact_import {"artifact_type": "TriangleSurfaceMesh", "path": "tests/fixtures/master/wave_a_boolean/cube_overlap.off", "unit": "mm"}
- $cube_contained: cgal_artifact_import {"artifact_type": "TriangleSurfaceMesh", "path": "tests/fixtures/master/wave_a_boolean/cube_contained.off", "unit": "mm"}
(Use your own file of the same artifact type and unit for real work.)

## Steps
1. `mesh.boolean.union` (union): Construct the exact volume union of two closed outward-oriented triangle surface meshes.
   inputs {"source_a": "$cube_a", "source_b": "$cube_overlap"}; parameters {"operation": "union"}
2. `mesh.boolean.difference` (diff): Construct source A minus source B as an exact bounded volume Boolean.
   inputs {"source_a": {"slot": "geometry", "step": "union"}, "source_b": "$cube_contained"}; parameters {"operation": "difference"}
3. `mesh.inspect.pmp` (inspect): Inspect raw OFF and constructible polygon-mesh health without repairing or mutating geometry.
   inputs {"mesh": {"slot": "geometry", "step": "diff"}}; parameters {}

## cgal_plan request
```json
{"request": {"steps": [{"id": "union", "inputs": {"source_a": "$cube_a", "source_b": "$cube_overlap"}, "operation": "mesh.boolean.union", "parameters": {"operation": "union"}}, {"id": "diff", "inputs": {"source_a": {"slot": "geometry", "step": "union"}, "source_b": "$cube_contained"}, "operation": "mesh.boolean.difference", "parameters": {"operation": "difference"}}, {"id": "inspect", "inputs": {"mesh": {"slot": "geometry", "step": "diff"}}, "operation": "mesh.inspect.pmp", "parameters": {}}]}}
```

## Expected outcome
job state `succeeded`; every inserted validator `pass`. Inspect job.outputs (type, unit, properties) and job.validation[].report.

